.TH MATT 1 "2026-11-11" "MATT 1.7.0" "MATT Manual"
.SH NAME
matt \- MAN AT THE TOP: authorized MITM credential capture and decode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B matt
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B matt --analyze-only
.I REPORT
.RI [ --pretty | --table | --json ]
.RI [ --crack ]
.br
.B sudo matt --iface
.I NAME
.B --i-have-written-authorization
.RI [ --no-poison ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B MATT
is a two-stage credential-recovery toolkit for authorized wireless
man-in-the-middle engagements. Stage one ARP-poisons the local segment
(ettercap) and sniffs it (tcpdump/tshark), reassembling each packet and writing a
deterministic
.IR capture_report.json .
Stage two decodes those bytes into hashcat-ready candidates and plain-English
findings, optionally cracking them.
.PP
MATT has no runtime dependencies (pure Python standard library). A default run
opens no socket and costs zero tokens; artificial intelligence is never required.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B matt
With no arguments in a terminal, open the interactive menu.
.TP
.B matt --analyze-only \fIREPORT\fR
Decode an existing capture report. No root, no interface, no network.
.TP
.B sudo matt --iface \fINAME\fR --i-have-written-authorization
Live ARP-poison capture. Add
.B --no-poison
for passive sniffing only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --pretty
Print one block per credential, source host to destination.
.TP
.B --table
Print one compact row per credential (host, target, user, type, secret).
.TP
.B --json
Print the analysis as JSON for piping into jq or other tools.
.TP
.B --crack
Run hashcat on the findings and show any recovered plaintext.
.TP
.B --wordlist \fIPATH\fR
Wordlist for --crack (default /usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt).
.TP
.B --identify \fIHASH\fR
Name a hash's likely type(s) and hashcat mode, and reverse it instantly if it is
a common password.
.TP
.B --watch \fIDIR\fR
Active response: watch a directory for new capture reports and analyze each as it
appears.
.TP
.B --use-model
Opt in to LLM-written prose. The only option that opens a socket.
.TP
.B --i-have-written-authorization
Required for a live run. Confirms written authorization for the network.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.SH SAFETY
A live run refuses to start unless the process is root, the
.B --iface
exists, and
.B --i-have-written-authorization
is given. Run only against networks you are authorized to test.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Analyze a capture and show a table:
.B matt --analyze-only capture_report.json --table
.TP
Identify and reverse a hash:
.B matt --identify 5f4dcc3b5aa765d61d8327deb882cf99
.TP
Live passive capture on Wi-Fi:
.B sudo matt --iface wlan0 --no-poison --i-have-written-authorization
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hashcat (1),
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR ettercap (8)
.PP
Full guides: README.md, USAGE.md, INSTALL.md in the MATT repository.
